---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Privacy Policy',
  },
];

const lastUpdated = '2026-10-06';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="LocalNodeOps privacy policy: cookieless aggregate analytics via Umami, no ad trackers, no server-side accounts."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="max-w-reading mx-auto px-lg py-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-display-hero text-primary">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-body-md text-secondary mt-xs">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        LocalNodeOps uses Umami Cloud for privacy-first analytics — aggregate
        page views, referral sources, and general device/browser category,
        with no personally identifiable information collected and no
        individual visitor profile built or stored. Umami does not use
        cookies, does not track visitors across other websites, and does
        not sell or share data with advertisers. We do not run
        session-recording tools, advertising trackers, or any script that
        identifies an individual visitor. There is no user account system
        and no server-side database of visitor activity beyond the
        aggregate analytics described here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Local storage</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        The only data this site stores directly on your device is a single
        <code>theme</code> value (light or dark) saved in your browser's
        <code>localStorage</code>. It stays on your device, is never
        transmitted to any server, and exists only to remember your display
        preference between visits. See the <a href="/cookies">Cookies
        page</a> for why this is technically not a cookie.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Hosting logs</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        Like any web host, our deployment platform (Vercel) may retain
        standard server access logs (IP address, request timestamp,
        requested path) for operational and security purposes. We do not
        access or process these logs for analytics or tracking.
      </p>
    </section>

      <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">AI assistant</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        If you use the optional chat assistant, the text you type is sent through our server to Google's Gemini API to generate a reply. On Google's free tier, Google may use submitted content to improve its products, and human reviewers may read it, so please do not enter personal, confidential or sensitive information. We do not save your messages and do not link them to an account, because the site has none. The assistant is not offered to visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland. Its answers can be wrong; use the calculator for exact figures.
      </p>
    </section>
    
    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Third-party links</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        Pages may link to external sites (documentation, hardware vendor
        pages, cloud GPU providers, affiliate partners, GitHub
        repositories). Those sites have their own privacy practices, which
        this policy does not cover.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        Questions about this policy can be sent to the address on the
        <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>